.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.PP
.nf
The match_hostname() function from Python 3\&.3\&.3, essential when using SSL\&.
.fi
.PP
 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "pip\&._vendor\&.urllib3\&.util\&.ssl_match_hostname\&._dnsname_match ( dn,  hostname,  max_wildcards = \fC1\fP)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Matching according to RFC 6125, section 6\&.4\&.3

http://tools\&.ietf\&.org/html/rfc6125#section-6\&.4\&.3

.fi
.PP
 
.SS "pip\&._vendor\&.urllib3\&.util\&.ssl_match_hostname\&._ipaddress_match ( ipname,  host_ip)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Exact matching of IP addresses\&.

RFC 6125 explicitly doesn't define an algorithm for this
(section 1\&.7\&.2 - 'Out of Scope')\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS "pip\&._vendor\&.urllib3\&.util\&.ssl_match_hostname\&._to_unicode ( obj)\fC [protected]\fP"

.SS "pip\&._vendor\&.urllib3\&.util\&.ssl_match_hostname\&.match_hostname ( cert,  hostname)"

.PP
.nf
Verify that *cert* (in decoded format as returned by
SSLSocket\&.getpeercert()) matches the *hostname*\&.  RFC 2818 and RFC 6125
rules are followed, but IP addresses are not accepted for *hostname*\&.

CertificateError is raised on failure\&. On success, the function
returns nothing\&.

.fi
.PP
 
